Your first priority should be to check the priests for cloaks of magic
resistance. You have a 1/10 chance per priest and it's easy to check
by zapping with wand of probing (or magic missile if you can safely
anger them). If you need to kill a priest of Kos then get a powerful
pet - it should be easy at this point.

Not having speed boots, a CoMR, or jumping boots most certainly merits
polypiling. I would never write identify scrolls after I found the
castle wand because polypiling produces *tons* of them. Get some elven
cloaks and boots from the first few levels of Gehennom, stock up on
enemies' scrolls of create monster (sit on a magic trap on the quest
and you'll get plenty of scrolls/potions from nymphs), and blank all
the scrolls you possibly can. Put no more than four items in a pile,
none cursed, for optimal results. You will most likely get enough
scrolls of enchant armor out of the process to finish enchanting your
armor if you start with twenty blank scrolls.

As for "no good helm", the elves you kill should likely net a +2 or +3
elven leather helm, which is more than sufficient.

If all else fails, zap a wand of create monster in Gehennom from the
upstairs on a burned E, and you'll probably get several dragons this
way. In the mazes, it's easy to find an upstairs with nearby walls for
defense.


